## 1. Overview

AWS Direct Connect is a cloud service that establishes a dedicated network connection from your premises to AWS. It enables you to establish consistent, low-latency connections to AWS and its resources using private network connectivity instead of traversing the public internet.

### Key Characteristics

- **Dedicated Connection** - Physical, private connection to AWS
- **Low Latency** - Consistent latency, no internet variability
- **High Bandwidth** - Up to 100 Gbps connection speeds
- **Network Isolation** - Private connectivity, no internet exposure
- **Cost Reduction** - Reduces data transfer costs vs internet
- **Consistent Performance** - Not subject to internet congestion
- **Business Continuity** - Reliable connectivity for critical workloads
- **Multiple Connection Types** - Dedicated, Hosted, Transit Gateway

### Direct Connect vs Internet VPN

| Feature | Direct Connect | Internet VPN |
|---------|---|---|
| Connection Type | Dedicated physical | Internet-based |
| Bandwidth | Up to 100 Gbps | Limited by ISP |
| Latency | Consistent (<50ms typical) | Variable (50-200ms+) |
| Setup Time | Weeks | Minutes |
| Cost | Higher monthly | Lower monthly |
| Reliability | 99.99% uptime SLA | ISP dependent |
| Security | Private network | Encrypted but internet |
| Throughput | Predictable | Bursty |
| Best For | Enterprise, critical workloads | SMB, non-critical |

