## 11. Best Practices

### Design Best Practices

✓ DO:
- Use LAG for redundancy (2+ connections minimum)
- Implement multiple locations for disaster recovery
- Configure BGP with backup internet connection
- Monitor connection health with CloudWatch alarms
- Use private VIFs for internal traffic
- Implement route filtering to prevent accidents
- Test failover scenarios regularly
- Document your network topology and BGP configuration
- Use Direct Connect Gateway for multi-region
- Consider MACsec for sensitive workloads

✗ DON'T:
- Rely on single connection for critical workloads
- Use 1 Gbps connections for production (upgrade to 10 Gbps)
- Configure symmetric BGP weights (leads to routing loops)
- Forget to update customer router firmware
- Ignore provider notifications about maintenance
- Run untested failover scenarios
- Use same VLAN for multiple VIFs (unless intentional)
- Over-provision without testing capacity
- Ignore latency monitoring
- Forget to configure alarm notifications

### Security Best Practices

```bash
