         │
    ┌────┼────┬─────────┐
    ↓    ↓    ↓         ↓
   VPC VPC  VPC       VPC
 (us) (eu) (apac)  (other)
```

**Benefits of DXG:**
✓ **Single connection** handles all regions
✓ **Centralized management** via AWS console
✓ **Dynamic routing** via BGP (no manual updates)
✓ **Automatic failover** if one path down
✓ **Cost efficient** - one connection for all
✓ **Simplified configuration** - fewer VIFs
✓ **Scalable** - add new regions without new DX

**Example Configuration:**

```bash
# Single DX connection
aws directconnect create-connection \
  --location "Equinix SV1" \
  --bandwidth "10Gbps" \
  --connection-name "dxg-primary"

# Create Direct Connect Gateway
aws directconnect create-direct-connect-gateway \
  --name "corporate-dxg"

# Create ONE Private VIF on DX → DXG
aws directconnect create-private-virtual-interface \
  --connection-id dxcon-xxx \
  --new-private-virtual-interface '{
    "virtualInterfaceName": "dxg-vif",
    "vlan": 100,
    "asn": 65000,
    "directConnectGatewayId": "dcgw-yyy"
  }'

# Associate Transit Gateways from each region
aws directconnect create-direct-connect-gateway-association \
  --direct-connect-gateway-id dcgw-yyy \
  --gateway-id tgw-us-east-1

aws directconnect create-direct-connect-gateway-association \
  --direct-connect-gateway-id dcgw-yyy \
  --gateway-id tgw-eu-west-1

aws directconnect create-direct-connect-gateway-association \
  --direct-connect-gateway-id dcgw-yyy \
  --gateway-id tgw-ap-southeast-1

# Result: On-premises can reach VPCs in all regions
# via single DX connection and single VIF!
```

**Approach 2: Traditional Routing (VGW per Region)**

```
Architecture:
┌────────────────────────────────────┐
│ On-Premises Data Center            │
└────┬───────────────────────────────┘
     │
     ├─ VIF to VGW (us-east) → us-east VPC
     ├─ VIF to VGW (eu-west) → eu-west VPC
     └─ VIF to VGW (ap-southeast) → ap-southeast VPC

     OR

     ├─ DX Connection 1 → us-east VGW
     ├─ DX Connection 2 → eu-west VGW
     └─ DX Connection 3 → ap-southeast VGW
```

**Limitations of Traditional Routing:**
✗ **Multiple VIFs needed** (one per VPC/region)
✗ **Multiple connections** required
✗ **Manual routing** - no inter-VPC through on-prem
✗ **Complex BGP** - manage many peers
✗ **Limited scalability** - new VPC = new connection
✗ **Higher cost** - multiple DX connections
✗ **Difficult management** - many VIFs to manage

**Comparison Matrix:**

| Aspect | Direct Connect Gateway | Traditional Routing |
|--------|------------------------|-------------------|
| Connections needed | 1 | N (one per region) |
| VIFs needed | 1 | N (one per region) |
| Cost (3 regions) | $300/month | $900+/month |
| Complexity | Simple | Complex |
| Scalability | Easy (add TGW) | Hard (need new DX) |
| Multi-VPC access | Yes (via TGW) | Limited (VPC per region) |
| BGP management | Single peer | Multiple peers |
| Failover | Automatic (TGW) | Manual per region |
| Setup time | Weeks (single DX) | Weeks × N |

**When to Use Each:**

**Use Direct Connect Gateway (Recommended for Most):**
- Multi-region applications
- Multiple VPCs per region
- Need inter-VPC communication
- Want to minimize cost
- Prefer simple management
- Building scalable infrastructure
- Future growth expected

**Use Traditional Routing (Legacy/Specific Cases):**
- Single VPC, single region
- Cannot use Transit Gateway (rare)
- Existing configuration (migration cost > benefit)
- Very specific routing requirements
- Old AWS accounts without TGW support

**Migration Path (Traditional → DXG):**

```
Phase 1: Create DXG and Transit Gateways
├─ Create Direct Connect Gateway
├─ Create Transit Gateways in each region
└─ Create TGW attachments to VPCs

Phase 2: Create new VIF to DXG
├─ Create Private VIF on DX → DXG
├─ Configure BGP on new VIF
└─ Monitor traffic via DXG

Phase 3: Gradual traffic migration
├─ Route some traffic through DXG
├─ Monitor performance and routing
└─ Adjust BGP weights as needed

Phase 4: Retire old VIFs
├─ Migrate remaining traffic to DXG
├─ Delete old VIFs
├─ Decommission old VGWs (if possible)
└─ Cost savings achieved

Duration: 2-4 weeks (no downtime)
```

